---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Services | Web Management, Marketing Strategy & Training" description="Web management, marketing strategy, training, and implementation. Monthly retainers, not hourly surprises.">
  <section class="relative pt-40 pb-24 px-6 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-[400px] h-[400px] bg-amber-500/5 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <p class="reveal text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-8">Services</p>
      <h1 class="reveal font-serif text-5xl md:text-7xl text-neutral-100 leading-[1.05] mb-10">
        Four things I do.
      </h1>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed">
        Monthly retainers, not hourly surprises. You pick the tier that fits. Everything is month-to-month after onboarding because if I'm not earning the next month, I shouldn't get it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Web Management -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/services/web-management" class="group">
        <h2 class="reveal font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100 mb-3 group-hover:text-amber-400 transition-colors duration-300">Web Management</h2>
      </a>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mt-8">
        <p class="reveal">
          Your site is probably on shared hosting you don't control, running plugins that haven't been updated in months, with no one watching if it goes down at 2am on a Saturday. You find out something broke when a customer mentions it. That's the problem I solve.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal">
          I take over the whole thing. Your site moves to dedicated cloud hosting under my management. I handle updates, security, backups, and monitoring. Every month you get a plain-language report showing exactly what happened and what's coming next. You stop worrying about it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal mt-10 glow-card p-6">
        <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-4">Includes</p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Site migration, dedicated cloud hosting, security monitoring and SSL, WordPress core and plugin updates, daily backups, uptime monitoring, and a monthly Site Health Report.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href="/services/web-management" class="reveal inline-flex items-center gap-3 text-amber-400 text-sm mt-8 hover:text-amber-300 transition-colors duration-300 group">
        Full details and pricing
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Marketing Strategy -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 dot-grid">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/services/marketing-strategy" class="group">
        <h2 class="reveal font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100 mb-3 group-hover:text-amber-400 transition-colors duration-300">Marketing Strategy</h2>
      </a>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mt-8">
        <p class="reveal">
          You know your marketing could be better. You just don't know where to start. There's SEO, content, ads, social, email, and twelve opinions about which one matters most. Meanwhile the site has no meta descriptions, your competitor is outranking you, and you can't tell if your traffic is going up or down because nobody set up the tracking right.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal">
          I sort through all of it and tell you what to do first. An SEO roadmap built on real keyword data. Competitive analysis that names names. Content briefs your writer can actually use. Monthly calls to keep it on track. I direct the strategy. You execute it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal mt-10 glow-card p-6">
        <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-4">Starts with</p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          A strategic audit. A full read of your site, your market, and your competitors. The findings become your roadmap. Then monthly direction, content briefs, and quarterly reporting with real numbers.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href="/services/marketing-strategy" class="reveal inline-flex items-center gap-3 text-amber-400 text-sm mt-8 hover:text-amber-300 transition-colors duration-300 group">
        Full details and pricing
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Implementation -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/services/implementation" class="group">
        <h2 class="reveal font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100 mb-3 group-hover:text-amber-400 transition-colors duration-300">Implementation</h2>
      </a>
      <div class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mt-8 space-y-5">
        <p>
          Your contact form submissions aren't reaching your CRM. Your analytics aren't tracking conversions. You need landing pages for a market you're entering but they don't exist yet. These are projects with a start, a scope, and a finish line. I scope it, quote it, build it, and hand it over.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal mt-10 grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="glow-card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-3">Integrations</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Form-to-CRM, analytics, email marketing, payment systems. The connections between your website and the tools your business actually runs on.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="glow-card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-3">Page builds</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Landing pages, service pages, content rewrites. The pages that need to exist for your marketing to work.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="glow-card p-6">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-3">Analytics setup</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">GA4, Search Console, conversion tracking. Configured so the data you see actually means something.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="/services/implementation" class="reveal inline-flex items-center gap-3 text-amber-400 text-sm mt-8 hover:text-amber-300 transition-colors duration-300 group">
        Full details and pricing
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Training -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/services/training" class="group">
        <h2 class="reveal font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100 mb-3 group-hover:text-amber-400 transition-colors duration-300">Training</h2>
      </a>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mt-8">
        <p class="reveal">
          Your team sat through a training webinar last year. They forgot 80% of it within a week. Now they still ask you to "update the website" because nobody actually learned how. The problem isn't your team. The problem is that one-shot training doesn't work.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal">
          I build guided programs. Three sessions over three to four weeks, with real assignments between them. Your team practices on their own systems, makes mistakes in a safe context, and comes back with questions that matter. Built on learning science, not slide decks. WordPress and SEO, or AI workflows.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href="/services/training" class="reveal inline-flex items-center gap-3 text-amber-400 text-sm mt-8 hover:text-amber-300 transition-colors duration-300 group">
        Full details and pricing
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="relative py-32 px-6 surface-1 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-[500px] h-[300px] bg-amber-500/5 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg mb-10">Not sure which of these fits? Tell me what's going on and I'll tell you. Sometimes the answer is "none of them, here's what you actually need."</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="reveal inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 bg-amber-500 text-neutral-950 font-semibold text-sm rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-400 transition-all duration-300 hover:shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(245,158,11,0.25)]">
        Let's talk
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
